/// newspeak-spec.pdf 6: a declaration that ends in a dot instead of a class
/// body is the mixin application it writes, and 6.2 makes that "a class I
/// with mixin M and superclass S". At a module's root the one clause the
/// root rule allows is <: Value, so this module's class is the level Value's
/// mixin adds to Object, named for the module and with its factory, new.
/// 3.3 makes "the enclosing object of a module definition" nil: the level's
/// own enclosing object is Value's, which Value's methods reach, and the
/// declaration's own is nil.
///
/// The module declares no member, so instantiating it succeeds and the
/// entry send, main:args:, is not understood -- by run, and by load of the
/// image build writes, which carries the root as that level.
class Spec6ABodyLessRootIsTheValueLevelItsClauseAdds = Object <: Value.
